From: ovis-tui <ovis-tui@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 08:31:18 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] fix(embed): refuse input typed during a recovery that
 still waits in the reader queue

The reader's events and the pane's run on separate channels: a paste read while a terminal recovered could reach the app after the recovered screen's paint had released input, and be sent. Under the input policy a recovered wire's first paint now tells the app, which refuses the keys, text, pastes and mouse input still queued from the reader, with the reconnect notice, and handles everything else as usual.
